id: pm-beads-je7c
title: Preserve opted-in Beads extensions with versioned sidecars and explicit loss reports
description: "Acceptance: unknown nested fields survive import/export; conflicting native mappings refuse; size and privacy limits apply before mutation. Provide typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON command output, documentation and public-tracker copy validation without git."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T19:31:11.967Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T19:47:24.916Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Unknown nested fields survive import/export; Conflicting native mappings refuse; Size and privacy limits apply before mutation
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T19:31:43.910Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against the current CLI and sibling packages: core extension custom fields provide schema-owned values; beads diff compares mapped fields, and snapshot reconciliation manages mapped fields and acknowledged bases. pm-csv owns tabular column mapping. None preserves explicitly selected opaque Beads extension objects. Design: portable schema-1 sidecar capture before ordinary import, restore after ordinary export, keyed by exact external ids. Reuse native import/export and SDK atomic file writing and host rendering; never duplicate tracker mutation, settings, locking or mappings. Reject native field selection and overlay collisions. Report every unselected extension occurrence as loss; enforce bounded JSON and privacy policy before any output write. Sidecars stay separate from tracker items and must travel with the JSONL snapshot."
  "2026-10-23T19:41:00.552Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabling the restore overlay alone makes the nested-object round-trip regression fail (exit 1); disabling the native-selector guard alone makes the native-name refusal regression fail (exit 1). Restored both implementations afterward. Real compiled CLI native import/export preserved both synthetic nested extension fixtures and one dependency with no git executable available. Public-data validation archived origin/main d9b4152 into a non-git scratch tracker made read-only; all 97 public items read completely, 97 native exports, 97 synthetic nested extension fields restored, 97 deliberately unselected fields reported dropped. Source and copied tracker unchanged. Native JSONL 62639 bytes; sidecar 12087 bytes; restored JSONL 71166 bytes; compact JSON receipt 260 bytes. Native conflict, differing overlay, privacy and size refusals verified. These extension values are synthetic fixtures layered on public records, not claimed as naturally occurring source extensions."
  "2026-10-23T19:42:27.606Z",codex-agent,"All three linked checks pass via pm test --run --progress: targeted compiled-host/SDK/flag/docstring suite 15/15 (zero skipped); typecheck plus docstring lint pass; read-only public tracker validation passes. Targeted sidecar coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions. No separate lint script is defined; the repository docstring gate is the local lint check. Full npm and Bun release checks are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix as requested because host CPU is saturated. The installed host is current 2026.10.23; tracker writes use the package-pinned SDK/CLI 2026.10.20 without changing its pin."
  "2026-10-23T19:44:40.499Z",codex-agent,"Final hardening rejects unsafe integer extensions before capture to prevent JSON-number precision loss, rejects cyclic SDK envelopes with a typed refusal, and bounds existing overlay values before canonical comparison. Local health has unrelated inherited findings: a global pm-github/host pin mismatch and the already tracked installer fence drift (pm-beads-v9r1). No history repair, installer work or dependency pin changes performed. Clean CI health and npm/Bun release gates are the requested full validation authority."
  "2026-10-23T19:46:28.320Z",codex-agent,"The initial CodeQL review identified polynomial backtracking in incomplete PEM-header screening. Replaced the header regex with linear substring checks and retained the other bounded checks; added a repeated-incomplete-header fixture. SDK restore now validates typed envelopes before JSON serialization, so Infinity/NaN/unsafe integers cannot be silently coerced. Regression suite and exact-head CI are rerun after these final changes."
  "2026-10-23T19:47:23.849Z",codex-agent,"After final numeric validation and linear privacy screening, linked checks pass again: 15 targeted tests, typecheck, docstring lint, and read-only public-data validation. Sidecar source coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. The initial CI revision passed both npm matrix release gates; the final pushed revision must pass npm and Bun plus CodeQL before handoff. Sidecar scope is explicitly opted-in unknown top-level fields with recursively retained JSON values; nested extras inside native mapped fields remain outside this contract."
